OnPush:


- But in this case, it’s a waste of time: ⚠️we know that if the pony doesn’t change, the template of
    the Pony doesn’t need to be checked. ⚠️Same thing for the Image: if the src input is the same,
    there is no need to recompute the image URL. So let’s switch these components to OnPush:

        🔥🔥Starting with v22, you can simply remove the changeDetection property from the
        decorator to use OnPush, since it’s the default strategy.
    
    Image Component:

        @Component({
            selector: 'ns-img',
            template: `
                <p>{{ check() }}</p>
                <img [src]="src()" />
            `,
            changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush
        })
        export class Image {
            readonly src = input.required<string>();
            protected check(): void {
                console.log('image component view checked');
            }
        }


    Pony Component:

        @Component({
            selector: 'ns-pony',
            template: `
                <p>{{ check() }}</p>
                <ns-img [src]="ponyImageUrl()" />
            `,
            imports: [Image],
            changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush
        })
        export class Pony {
            readonly ponyModel = input.required<PonyModel>();
            protected readonly ponyImageUrl = computed(() => `images/pony-${this.ponyModel
                ().color}-running.gif`);

            protected check(): void {
                console.log('pony component view checked');
            }
        }
    

    Race component:

        @Component({
            selector: 'ns-race',
            template: `
                <h2>Race</h2>
                <p>{{ check() }}</p>
                @for (pony of ponies(); track pony.id) {
                    <div>
                        <ns-pony [ponyModel]="pony" />
                    </div>
                }
                <button (click)="changeColor()">Change color</button>
            `,
            imports: [Pony],
            changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.Eager 
        })
        export class Race {
            protected readonly ponies = signal<Array<PonyModel>>([
                { id: 1, color: 'green' },
                { id: 2, color: 'orange' }
            ]);
            protected readonly colors: Array<string> = ['green', 'orange', 'blue'];

            protected check(): void {
                console.log('race component view checked');
            }

            protected changeColor(): void {
                const ponies = this.ponies();
                ponies[0].color = this.randomColor();   // change color of the first pony
                this.ponies.set([...ponies]);
            }
        }


    🔥🔥When we click to change the color, we will only see in the console:
        
        race component view checked

    Which is awesome, because it means that we don’t check the components that we don’t need to
    check \o/.


